<title>DUBAI: Union National Bank gives first result since BCCI.</title>
<headline>Union National Bank gives first result since BCCI.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five years and six months to June 30, 1996 versus year to December 31, 1990</p>
<p>		    (million dirhams unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit		  74.716	vs     52.976</p>
<p>Net interest income    646.377	vs    105.136</p>
<p>Net operating income   938.329	vs    167.444</p>
<p>Provisions		 289.872	vs     28.00</p>
<p>Retained earnings - at</p>
<p>beginning of period	0.382	vs	0.103</p>
<p>- at end of period</p>
<p>				60.154	vs	0.382</p>
<p>Proposed total</p>
<p>dividend			 none     vs     29.044</p>
<p>Assets			 5.48 bln   vs  5.76 bln</p>
<p>Loans and advances	 3.73 bln  vs  3.11 bln</p>
<p>Customers' deposits	4.84 bln  vs  5.09 bln</p>
<p>Full name: Union National Bank, formerly Bank of Credit and Commerce (Emirates).</p>
<p>NOTE: These results are the first submitted to shareholders for approval since the collapse in July 1991 of majority shareholder Bank of Credit and Commerce International (BCCI).</p>
<p>The Department of Finance of the Abu Dhabi government recently acquired BCCI's 40 percent stake in the bank.</p>
<p>Listed among &quot;other assets&quot; is 310.929 million dirhams as the net amount due from BCCI group liquidators at end-June 1996.</p>
<p>A figure of 36.810 million dirhams, which at end-1990 was listed as goodwill, has been written off.  -- Dubai newsroom +9714-626990</p>
</text>
